# Surfaces

Separate regions with the first tool that works. Stop there:

1. Gap or spacing
2. Color or opacity
3. Visual weight
4. Font size or weight
5. A light background fill
6. A border
7. A divider — only when spacing cannot show the boundary, such as a dense table

A border plus a background is one raised level. Use at most one raised region per screen (a movable card or a single focal panel), and pair it with a shadow. Do not nest a bordered filled card inside another. Group the rest with spacing, one border, or a light fill.

A page, section, panel, dialog, or list row gets a title or a description, never both. If both feel necessary, merge them into one line.

```tsx
// ❌ nested cards, and a kicker that repeats the heading
<section className="rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
  <p className="text-xs font-semibold uppercase">Shopper</p>
  <h2 className="text-xl font-semibold">Returning shopper</h2>
  <div className="mt-3 rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-3">…</div>
</section>

// ✅ one heading, related items grouped by gap
<section className="py-8">
  <h2 className="text-xl font-semibold text-indigo-950">Returning shopper</h2>
  <dl className="mt-4 flex gap-6 text-sm text-stone-600">…</dl>
</section>
```
